      "writtenOn": "2025-05-28T22:09:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e uint32 Count w2\n• If Bit[0] \u003d b’0 in the Flags input parameter, this field contains the count of partition information descriptors corresponding to the specified UUID in w1-w4. The descriptors are populated in the RX buffer of the caller.\n• If Bit[0] \u003d b’1 in the Flags input parameter, this field contains the count of partitions deployed in the system corresponding to the specified UUID in w1-w4.\n\nIn either case, `count \u003d\u003d res-\u003ea2 \u003d\u003d 0` means that there are no descriptors in the buffer. The spec doesn\u0027t say what happens to the RX buffer in that case, but all current implementations skip the transfer.",
      "parentUuid": "1a7d48f5_1167e019",
      "revId": "d144c7c1855f43fd12a95ea61ad33e1a2d319f27",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
